<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Diagnose</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Assassin (guild level 0, up to 60%), Barbarian (guild level 0), Conjurer (guild level 0, up to 80%), Dark Knight (guild level 1, up to 70%), Druid (guild level 0, up to 85%), Fighter (guild level 0), Healer (guild level 0), Necromancer (guild level 5, up to 75%), Paladin (guild level 1, up to 70%), Ranger (guild level 1, up to 70%), Thief (guild level 4, up to 70%)
Also taught by: Gustav, in the back room of the inn in Udgaard (anyone, up to 35%); Mary the Lumberjack Wife, in her cabin in the forest of Haon-Dor (to those who have brought back her cooking pot, up to 50%); Brother Johannes, at the monastery in the vineyards near Nymgaard (from level 40)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>diagnose &lt;character&gt;
diagnose                (whoever you are fighting)
</pre>
<p>Tells you how badly hurt someone is, from "in an excellent condition" to 
"bleeding awfully from big wounds". It works on friends and foes alike, and 
in the middle of a fight: with no name, you diagnose the one you are 
fighting. Outside a fight you also see how heavy and how tall they are.
</p><p>Your skill and your brain decide how true the answer is: when you misjudge, 
they look healthier than they really are.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
